Article 2 (Scope of Producers' Organizations)
"Organizations meeting the requirements prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries" in Article 4, subparagraph 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on Fisheries and Fishing Villages Development (hereinafter referred to as the "Decree") means the following organizations:
1. An incorporated fishery cooperative under Article 16 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities with capital of at least 100 million won;
2. An incorporated fisheries company under Article 19 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities that meets all of the following requirements:
(a) At least five fishers participate as members, shareholders, etc.;
(b) Capital is at least 100 million won;
3. A self-help fund organization under Article 2, subparagraph 3 of the Act on the Creation and Operation of Agricultural and Fishery Self-Help Funds that creates and operates a fishery self-help fund pursuant to Article 3 of the same Act;
4. A cooperative or social cooperative established under the Framework Act on Cooperatives with capital of at least 100 million won;
5. A federation of cooperatives or federation of social cooperatives established under the Framework Act on Cooperatives that meets all of the following requirements:
(a) Its members include cooperatives or social cooperatives under subparagraph 4;
(b) Its capital is at least 100 million won;
6. A salt producers' cooperative established under the Salt Producers' Cooperative Act.
